    <string name="about_name_heading">To hear. To listen. To take something to heart.</string>
    <string name="about_name_body">In Hawaiian, that is Lohe (lōhe). We built the app around the simple idea of listening on your own terms. Whether you are into gripping stories, honest conversations, the daily news, or a deep dive on a random obsession, Lohe lets you hear what you want, exactly how you want to hear it. It stays out of your way and remembers where you left off.\n\nUa lohe ʻoe?</string>
    <string name="about_kani_heading">Kani</string>
    <string name="about_kani_body">That little dragonfly on your home screen is Kani. His name comes from the Hawaiian idea of listening with quiet, focused attention. He keeps an eye on your library so your next listen is always ready when you are.</string>
